    "blurb": "Consolidate and manage tasks across systems",
    "overview": "KADAI is an open-source Java library that consolidates tasks from Camunda 8, Camunda 7, and other systems into a single enterprise-grade tasklist. It provides dynamic prioritization, workbasket-based routing, fine-grained access control, and real-time monitoring for large-scale task management operations.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Consolidate every Camunda task into one enterprise-grade tasklist",
    "splashDescription": "Large organizations running Camunda often need more control over task management than a standard tasklist provides — dynamic prioritization, workbasket-based routing, fine-grained access control, and real-time monitoring across teams and systems. KADAI is an open-source Java library that consolidates tasks from Camunda 8, Camunda 7, and other external systems into a single unified tasklist using a flexible adapter architecture. It can run standalone or be embedded into your own application, with extensive configuration options and service provider interfaces that let you adapt routing logic, priority calculations, and security integration to your exact requirements. KADAI is already deployed by large insurance companies serving up to 5,000 users, giving it the production-proven track record to support ambitious enterprise implementations.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/808029/overview/img15691545693432376420.png?991a054adc307001eb79d61a79c822f5",
